WEBVTT

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.640
<i>It is the 25th year of the Taisho Era.</i>

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.510
<b>Purgatory Island Murder Case
Moritsune Saichou</b>

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.130
<i>A series of murders has 
claimed women's lives.</i>

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.730
<i>Suspected of being related to the incidents,</i>

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.530
<i>Shizuru is detained by the police.</i>

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.650
<i>Believing in his innocence, 
the girl works quickly</i>

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:15.440
<i>to catch the true killer, 
and the case is solved.</i>

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.160
<i>That night, Shizuru looks over a certain 
manuscript and loses himself in thought.</i>

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.870
<i>Is it his teacher's manuscript, 
which he claimed he'd discarded?</i>

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.530
<i>This is the story of Kuze 
Tsugumi and her kindness.</i>

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:04.680
It's such a soft color.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:06.190
How beautiful.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:11.480
I acquired it specifically because
I thought you might like it.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.280
I do. I'd like to have this, Kuina-san.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.190
Thank you!

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.920
It's a raw jade stone, isn't it?

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.000
Yes. I love them, so I collect them.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.470
I guess it's because they 
share a name with me.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:29.910
Thanks, Perry.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.710
I also collect kingfisher feathers.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:38.100
Because it's written with 
the same kanji as your name?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:40.300
That's right.

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:47.220
Mother's Face

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.220
-Kingfisher-

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:51.980
By the way, this is a bit 
difficult to admit to you,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.980
but a bargain got away from me.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.500
Apparently a man came here last night 
 to sell a Japanese-style book,

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.460
but because I wasn't here, 
he took it to another shop.

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:07.680
Was it a cursed tome?

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:12.370
I'm not sure, but there was 
something curious about it.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.670
It was apparently written by 
a prostitute in Yokohama.

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:20.410
A prostitute in Yokohama?

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:22.680
That is certainly rare.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:24.010
Is it?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:29.770
Many things are discarded 
or sold as a result of poverty.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.880
Being able to write a book
at all is rare in and of itself.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.820
It makes me wonder what the book is about.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.070
Do you know what store bought it?

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.030
I already sold that book.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.780
To whom? Who did you sell it to?

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.900
I can't give away a client's 
personal information.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:54.790
Though if you have a warrant, 
that's a different story.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.660
But...

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:58.840
First of all, it wasn't a cursed tome.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:00.600
But I want to know!

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:03.050
You never quit, do you?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.260
Why don't you go search 
for cursed tomes, then?

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:10.890
After all, a number of people 
died in the recent Migiwa case

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:14.230
because you all aren't working hard enough.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:20.020
Sasagoi-san is as ruthless as ever,

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:24.260
but he's right that we need to work harder.

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.080
Hisui?

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.720
Huh? Oh, what is it?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:32.080
Oh, it's not a big deal.

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.120
Um...

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.330
Well, well. Hoshikawa-kun.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.050
Professor Mozuyama...

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:41.840
And how are you?

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:45.590
<i>That's... the man from back then!</i>

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:49.120
You seem to be working hard at your job.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.240
But be careful you don't 
carelessly burn your friends.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.960
I've been searching for your 
replacement all this time,

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.370
but I just can't find one.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:02.990
Excuse me, but who are you?

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:07.130
I am Mozuyama, a professor at 
the Imperial Capital University.

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.490
How about it? Would you care 
to come visit my laboratory?

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:14.750
Stop it! She has nothing to do with this!

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:17.810
Goodness me, so scary.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:20.000
Well, then, I will take my leave.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.760
Hisui?

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.760
Don't get involved with him. 
Never, no matter what!

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.020
This is so good!

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.640
Hey! Kuze, Hisui, welcome back!

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.400
Come on, you two. Hurry over here.

00:05:41.260 --> 00:05:43.400
There are so many rice crackers!

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.500
My grandmother made them herself.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.660
She sells them at a shop in Asakusa.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.360
I see!

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:51.320
Have some.

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:52.410
With pleasure.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:56.910
Delicious!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.870
I'm so glad.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.040
Man, this aroma is the best.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.920
Hayato, are you going to hog 
all the seaweed ones?

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.550
You caught on, huh?

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.360
Fine, then. I'll split it with you.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.520
No, thanks. I prefer the green laver ones.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.460
Nah, the sugar crackers are the best.

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.690
They're a brilliant, thrilling 
harmony of salty and sweet.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:23.210
Thrilling?

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.190
That's just a bit nonsensical, Shizuru-san.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:27.200
Seaweed!

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:27.850
Green laver!

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:28.820
Sugar!

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:33.360
So this is miso-flavored? 
Commoner food is so profound.

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:34.990
Well said, young master.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:36.450
Don't call me that!

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.820
In addition to roasted rice crackers,

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.300
there are also fried varieties.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:44.710
They are delicious as well, so you
should try them someday.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.360
There's no end to Kijitani-san's 
random knowledge.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:50.660
Incidentally, I read in a book that there
are even deer rice crackers they sell

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:52.220
He even knows more than me,
a grandson of a rice cracker seller.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.970
at Nara Park for feeding the deer there.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:06:55.750
It seems that book was not wrong.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:57.010
<i>Hisui...</i>

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:00.480
On your own today, princess?

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:03.480
Well, I'm not on patrol.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:05.980
I'm worried about Hisui.

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:08.990
I see.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:13.000
He's still worried about that
Japanese-style book.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.750
Because the prostitute from Yokohama 
is just like his missing mother, I bet.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:19.750
Huh?

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.750
You didn't hear about it from Shiori yet?

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:26.250
No.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:30.510
<i>Being a sheltered young lady,
you may not be aware of this,</i>

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.210
<i>but you know how there are many ships 
that sail into Yokohama from overseas?</i>

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:39.450
<i>Well, that resulted in several red light 
districts that cater to foreigners.</i>

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:41.270
<i>That's where Hisui was born.</i>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:47.270
The color of his eyes and hair are 
because he's the child of a foreigner.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.530
<i>I had no idea...</i>

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:52.000
<i>I wasn't aware of any of that.</i>

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:55.570
<i>I just thought his eyes 
and hair were beautiful.</i>

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:03.040
Hisui probably thinks there's something 
written about his mother in that book.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:14.300
It really is you, Kuze Tsugumi-san.

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.930
Shiginuma Shouko-san?

00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:20.530
When I saw you, I thought it might be you.

00:08:20.530 --> 00:08:21.660
Good day.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.420
G-Good day.

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:25.580
I can't help but think that

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.330
running into you here must be fate,
and not mere coincidence.

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:35.820
I heard that your companion was 
interested in a certain book.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.330
I'm the one who purchased that book.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:41.590
Huh?

00:08:41.590 --> 00:08:44.850
Say, why don't you come to my room?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.460
I'm sorry. I'll take it off now.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.270
I asked you to wear the 
blindfold for your own sake.

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.730
There are many things here at Nachtigal 
that you are better off not seeing.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:09.170
I had been hoping to speak with you

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:12.540
ever since we met at the 
ball the other night.

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:16.490
Um, pardon me, but I'd like 
to know about the book...

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.200
Don't rush things.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:28.500
These are sugar candies I had
imported from France.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:33.510
They are as beautiful as jewels 
and as sweet as romance.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.010
Here.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.080
<i>Its elegant sweetness so quickly melts 
and spreads throughout my mouth.</i>

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.210
You are quite remarkable.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:51.150
Making use of the power you have 
in a job finding cursed tomes.

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.820
Takashi-san, my husband, told me about it.

00:09:56.840 --> 00:09:59.200
He knows everything.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.190
Yes, absolutely everything.

00:10:02.190 --> 00:10:05.160
He is very kind to me, but...

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:06.460
But?

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:13.170
Well, shall we change the subject?

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:18.690
To the topic you've been dying
to ask me about: that book.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:19.800
Yes!

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:23.330
I'm only partway through reading it,

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:27.180
but it's the diary of a prostitute from
a red light district in Yokohama.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.660
A diary?

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:30.440
Yes.

00:10:30.680 --> 00:10:34.130
Reading it warms the heart.

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.070
There are even fairy tales written in it.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:41.170
Like "The Robin's Dream" and 
"The Kingfisher Postman."

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.450
They are very sweet stories.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:44.950
Kingfisher...

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:50.710
Um, would you please consider 
giving me that diary?

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.760
I swear to you that it isn't a cursed tome.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.960
I want to let an acquaintance read it.

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.020
It could be about his mother...

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:01.580
I will not.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:06.100
It is a very precious diary to me, as well.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.740
Then could I at least borrow it?

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:21.760
Have you ever looked into a kaleidoscope?

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:23.370
Huh? Yes...

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:29.220
A friend of mine made them.

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:30.120
I see.

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:36.380
You know, I used to love kaleidoscopes.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.260
But now, I hate them.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:44.930
The beautiful shapes you love the most 
never come back a second time.

00:11:46.940 --> 00:11:48.390
I will consider it.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.010
Letting you borrow the diary.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:54.540
I truly appreciate it!

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.320
In exchange, come visit me again.

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:00.530
If you show them this,

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:04.030
you can come through the entrance 
hall without giving your name.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.980
But...

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:08.290
Please, let's be friends.

00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:13.600
I want you to remember this. 
As long as you do not betray me,

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:16.040
I will not betray you.

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.300
What's this?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.550
Do you intend to tame the 
inexperienced girl from Fukurou

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:32.060
and win her over as your friend?

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:36.680
As if I would consider
something so disgraceful.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:41.070
I told you never to appear before me again.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:48.580
Shouko-san, that noble pride of yours... 
You haven't changed a bit.

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:59.860
<i>You're a small bird with beautiful 
wings that will fly you anywhere.</i>

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:07.090
<i>Therefore, I pray you will treasure those
wings and never let anyone sully them.</i>

00:13:18.850 --> 00:13:21.520
<i>I went with her without thinking.</i>

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:25.030
<i>When she gave me that look,
for some reason, I just...</i>

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.450
Come visit me again.

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:33.950
<i>I can't go there again, but I want 
Hisui to be able to read that book.</i>

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.550
That's pretty.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:50.920
I was surprised the first time I saw it,

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:52.830
but it really is beautiful.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.440
I'm not so sure.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:57.400
I think it's actually rather ugly.

00:13:58.200 --> 00:13:59.920
That's not true.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:03.820
I was raised in a red light 
district in Yokohama.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:08.790
I always had to wear women's 
clothing when I was little.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:12.180
One day, a really drunk customer

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.080
tried to force himself on me...

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:19.940
That's when this power awakened.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:29.090
Fortunately, people from the brothel 
rushed in and saved the man...

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:35.720
But I still can't forgive myself for becoming 
an ugly person who would try to kill a man.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.400
This eye that has been stained 
red is the mark of my sin.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.480
It's ugly... It's so very ugly.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.060
No, that's not true at all.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:51.310
After a while, my mother disappeared 
without saying anything.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.990
She probably ran away from me.

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:58.340
Hisui, I...

00:14:58.340 --> 00:14:59.430
I'm sorry.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:03.280
I've made you worry about me all this time.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:09.600
That's why I wanted... 
I wanted to tell you everything.

00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:14.500
Also, please be careful 
around Professor Mozuyama.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.950
He has a very deep interest in my ability.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:21.080
He tried to experiment on me.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.260
That's awful.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.500
Kingfishers don't come here.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:34.280
Up until that incident, 
my mother was very kind.

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.900
She often used to tell me fairy tales.

00:15:37.900 --> 00:15:38.900
Fairy tales?

00:15:38.900 --> 00:15:44.140
Yes. My favorite was a story 
called "The Kingfisher Postman."

00:15:44.140 --> 00:15:47.050
"The Kingfisher Postman"?

00:15:47.050 --> 00:15:48.320
Hisui...

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:51.120
Listen, today I—

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:52.300
Kuze!

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.400
I need to speak with you.

00:15:56.520 --> 00:15:58.810
I heard from Yoshikiri-san a bit ago.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.720
He said he saw you get into 
Shiginuma Shouko's car today.

00:16:04.390 --> 00:16:05.940
Is that true?

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:08.190
It is.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:09.680
Why?

00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:11.210
I can't say why.

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:12.450
You can't say?

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.860
It's a personal matter.

00:16:14.860 --> 00:16:18.200
Tell me why. I won't accept excuses.

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:20.180
I'm serious.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:24.090
Depending on the circumstances, 
I may have to punish you severely.

00:16:24.640 --> 00:16:27.080
You might even have to leave here.

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.480
I-I...

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.720
Shiori-san, I know it's because of me!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:39.220
Kuina-san looked into it for me. He found out
 that Shiginuma Shouko bought that book.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:43.190
That's why I had given up on it.

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:48.020
So why? Why would you 
do something so risky?

00:16:48.020 --> 00:16:52.110
I'm sorry, but I just...

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.610
I understand the situation.

00:16:56.920 --> 00:17:01.620
<i>Listen, Kuze. Don't try to do anything 
so risky by yourself ever again.</i>

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:05.690
<i>My mother disappeared 
without saying anything.</i>

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:09.380
She probably ran away from me.

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:12.510
Reading it warms the heart.

00:17:21.130 --> 00:17:25.390
Even after Shiori-san warned you, 
why are you doing this?

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:29.360
I really want you to read that book.

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.210
No, I've already...

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.650
"The Kingfisher Postman."

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:38.640
"The Kingfisher Postman" 
is written in that book.

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:41.660
It has to be your mother's work!

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:45.840
That's why I have to...

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:49.250
You insist on meddling
for someone like me?

00:17:49.890 --> 00:17:52.170
You treat me as kindly as a little brother.

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:55.810
Please don't treat me 
like I'm younger than you.

00:17:56.920 --> 00:17:58.180
I'm going with you.

00:17:58.640 --> 00:18:03.430
If anything happens, I will protect you.

00:18:03.760 --> 00:18:04.640
Okay.

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:14.440
Hiwako!

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.380
You look just like Hiwako.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.200
Almost an exact copy.

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:24.200
Hiwako was my mother's name... 
But how do you know her?

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:28.170
We were best friends at the all-girls school.

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.980
Hiwako was also from a noble family,

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:39.130
but her family fell into ruin, and her 
parents passed away in succession.

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.970
To care for her younger siblings
who were still very small,

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.970
she sold her body.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.760
My mother had siblings?

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:51.980
I didn't know... I never heard 
anything about that.

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:54.880
She probably kept it from you deliberately.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.200
When she left home,

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.240
she knew that she would be 
entering a different life,

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:02.240
so she cut all her old ties.

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:05.400
Hiwako strengthened her resolve and chose

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.050
a path that meant sacrificing herself.

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:11.760
That's how kind she was.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:18.010
She would never hesitate to sacrifice 
herself to protect those she held most dear.

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:21.960
Then my mother completely changed.

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:25.360
My mother ran away and left me.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.770
From me, from my power...

00:19:28.240 --> 00:19:32.340
Because I'm ugly... ugly...

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:33.160
Hisui...

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:33.960
No!

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:37.710
No. She wasn't like that.

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:43.860
If you read this, you'll 
understand how she felt

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:47.850
and how much she loved and treasured you.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:56.290
<i>An aura?</i>

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:12.360
Hisui, my beloved child.

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:17.510
I want you to be happier than 
anyone else in the world.

00:20:20.840 --> 00:20:22.080
Mom?

00:20:26.570 --> 00:20:30.130
Mom... Mom! Mom!

00:20:30.650 --> 00:20:31.950
Mom!

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.700
Mom...

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:06.700
<i>I wanted to be friends with you,</i>

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:08.870
<i>but I'm afraid the situation has changed.</i>

00:21:09.270 --> 00:21:12.580
You cannot come here anymore, understand?

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:14.370
Not ever.

00:21:17.030 --> 00:21:18.620
Thank you.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:24.230
I was finally able to learn how my 
mother truly felt, thanks to you.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:25.770
But...

00:21:26.630 --> 00:21:31.390
Please... Please don't ever do 
anything so dangerous again.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:32.890
Hisui...

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:34.890
Please.

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:37.400
Okay.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:44.900
But knowing you, you'll probably do 
something dangerous again anyway.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:47.460
When that happens,

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:52.910
I will protect you. 
With my whole body and soul.

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:05.800
We can obtain everything we want,

00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:08.800
with our own hands.

00:23:20.550 --> 00:23:22.110
<i>This is Hoshikawa Hisui.</i>

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:36.510
Chapter 7:  "Movie Theater After the Rain -Tears-"

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:24.310
<i>Thank you so much for today.</i>

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:27.160
<i>I feel like I got to see 
my mother thanks to you.</i>

00:23:27.160 --> 00:23:29.020
<i>It was a wonderful time.</i>

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:32.800
<i>Karasu seems to have 
started plotting something.</i>

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>Please let me know if anything happens.</i>

00:23:35.500 --> 00:23:38.750
<i>I want to be the one to protect you.</i>
